TYPES.md §5.2, §8.2, §1: a field whose declared type holds the error type is not required: a record literal or a bare case leaving it out draws no E3302; its own finding stands alone. A field that is genuinely required and missing is still E3302, once (`r2`).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record R {
  a: Nope
  xs: [Nope2]
  b: Int
}

local let r: R = { b: 1 }

local let r2: R = {}

local variant V {
  one { c: Nope3 }
  two
}

local let v: V = one
-- findings.txt --
error[E2102]  a/a.canon:4:6
  unknown name Nope

error[E2102]  a/a.canon:5:8
  unknown name Nope2

error[E3302]  a/a.canon:11:19
  a.R needs field b

error[E2102]  a/a.canon:14:12
  unknown name Nope3

4 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
